WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:07.760
[12 Days of Christmas Instrumental Music]

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:12.660
So on the ninth day of Christmas

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:14.460
is something special to me

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.980
because it was a present from my daughter.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.640
She gave it to me at my grandson's birthday party

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.200
because our birthdays are very close together.

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:29.080
And it's a Periodic Table handkerchief.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:34.380
Not a very big handkerchief, but big enough to be useful.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:38.420
Unfortunately it doesn't have some of the later elements

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:42.580
but you could argue if you're 
going to blow your nose on it

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:46.120
perhaps it's just as well that it's not too up-to-date!

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:52.260
But I think it is quite fun, and it's very clear

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:55.260
compared to some of the other
Periodic Tables that you get.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:58.220
And it's really good, because you can hear from my voice

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:02.080
I've got a cold, so... here goes.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:03.380
(blows nose)

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:06.340
[Brady, laughing]
Professor, are you a hankie user?

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:07.880
Oh! Very much so.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:10.620
I always have two: one in each pocket.

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:13.940
Otherwise I sneeze in the most embarrassing way.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:17.040
I've always had handkerchiefs since I was a child,

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.420
and I used to wipe up the chemicals 
with my handkerchief.

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:25.840
And when I was at school one day

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:31.460
in the chapel, in the prayers, 
I pulled my handkerchief out of the pocket

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:35.140
and it just turned to powder! Because the chemicals

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:37.080
had all rotted it away

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:42.120
So nowadays I don't mop up my chemicals
with my handkerchief.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:43.820
On Day Nine:

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:47.860
we have a Periodic Table handkerchief,

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:52.380
a charred piece of wood, Day 7: a fan from a fan,

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:55.400
carbon, anthracite, a glowing plectrum,

00:01:55.400 --> 00:02:01.160
4 drinking receptacles, 2 periodic table bedcovers,

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:05.240
and one piece of tartaric acid from a Swiss wine barrel.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:07.780
What will be Day Ten?

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:14.540
[Music, "We Wish You a Merry Christmas"]

